 kept: {
  as: checkpoint,
  why: "JointTiming's walk battery, the comparison's step 4 on the box: walk's four CADENCE exports at jab c804ccb (CADENCE ad2f50b1, with TIMING 1e1388b0, with PREPARE 32b2dcd1, with PREPARE and TIMING 088eff5d, landed in runs/kernel/export/20261020-baselines) on P0's and P2's kernels exported at jab 73660a8 (landed as runs/kernel/export/20261020-jointtiming), headless and unprobed through walk's wrapper, through jab-stress's walk_battery runner from 16:26 to 18:29: twenty batches of three runs at walk's fixed seed, each target's on conditions in arm order, P0 await, P2 await, P2 prepare, then the off conditions, P0 await and P2 prepare, the off reversed, and the on reversed, 1KA1 then 1KB1, six runs a condition. Read guest-only by the timing selector's readings assembler at jab-stress 1e956e7 over jab 8807a33: all 60 valid and deciding at eps 3,700; P0 await's K violations 6,983 to 7,188 a run and P2's none in either order; the presented interval's median 16.66 to 16.69 ms for P0 await and P2 prepare, TIMING on or off, and 27.3 to 28.7 ms for P2 await, the await order's P + w + D; its 95th 17.9 to 20.1 ms for P0 await, 16.73 to 16.79 ms for P2 prepare, and 30.1 to 30.9 ms for P2 await; the TIMING control passing for P2 prepare and failing for P0 await on both targets, so P0 await's phases read instrumented-only. The batches' runs archived; the exports' provenance in their landed runs. Decided with the other batteries by runs/kernel/jointtiming/20261020T211529-decision. Cited by the kernel subiter's plan/agenda/FourHarts/PresentationContract/JointTiming.md. Revised for WalkIsolation: 1KA1's thirty runs are complete and valid, but twenty-four of them overlap research's concurrent file writes on the box, 16:25:57 to 17:15:23, every deciding TIMING-off run among them, and a twenty-fifth its commit and push at 17:15:37 to 17:15:38, so 1KA1's walk comparison is contaminated and decides nothing, and the TIMING controls built on those runs cannot establish their reading. The six runs of the last two 1KA1 batches, from 17:15:31, and 1KB1's thirty, 17:27:52 to 18:29:32, came after the file writes, so this overlap invalidates none of their figures, though it certifies no quiet machine for them either. Every stream stays complete and valid and every K observation stands. The runs used the spec table before SpecRamCarry, 1KA1 at 4 GiB and 1KB1 at 8 GiB."
 },
